        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.056,
            0.084,
            0.113,
            0.101
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Note"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.057,
            0.106,
            0.198,
            0.186
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The charges on the ions are not indicated in the formula of the compound."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.228,
            0.087,
            0.842,
            0.106
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Write the charges under the symbols rather than as superscripts."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.224,
            0.107,
            0.888,
            0.143
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) Crossover the charges (only the numbers) as shown below to obtain the formula."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.225,
            0.145,
            0.89,
            0.232
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) The chemical formula gives the simplest ratio of the elements in a compound. Therefore, after criss-crossing, the subscripts are divided by a common factor, if any. For example, if we get the subscripts 2 and 4, they are divided by 2 to get 1 and 2, which are then used as subscripts in the formula."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.221,
            0.244,
            0.329,
            0.263
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Examples"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.212,
            0.268,
            0.527,
            0.287
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The formula of calcium chloride"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.213,
            0.289,
            0.287,
            0.309
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Symbol"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.213,
            0.324,
            0.283,
            0.344
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Charge"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.328,
            0.289,
            0.459,
            0.341
          ],
          "content": [
            {
