        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.538,
            0.525,
            0.858,
            0.595
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Here, the valencies of the two elements are the same. We arrive at the formula "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { M g _ { 2 } O _ { 2 } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " but it is simply written as MgO."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.223,
            0.618,
            0.888,
            0.654
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This method can also be used to write formulae of compounds of metals with other polyatomic ions, such as calcium carbonate."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.222,
            0.656,
            0.888,
            0.709
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "For magnesium hydroxide, we write the symbol of the cation "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( \\mathrm { M g ^ { 2 + } } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " first, followed by the symbol of the anion (OH–). Then, their charges (only the numbers) are criss-crossed to get the formula."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 25,
          "bbox": [
            0.203,
            0.72,
            0.312,
            0.74
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Examples"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
